{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 1.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.2,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.75,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: this dispute is about the S$5.00 no-show fee on trip TRIP-2026-09945. I find the driver did wait at the pickup, but I find the fee was charged above what the schedule allows. The driver's side is made out. The trip record shows the driver marking 'arrived' at 08:43:00 and terminating at 08:51:00 with reason RIDER_NO_SHOW - an eight-minute hold against the 300-second (five-minute) STANDARD-zone minimum. The chat log, a complete contemporaneous record of the same window, shows the same thing independently: the driver at the lobby at 08:43:00, giving his car and plate at 08:45:20, an unanswered in-app call at 08:47:05, and a warning before he cancelled at 08:50:45; the rider sent no message and did not answer the call. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00901) is impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08(b) - it carries gaps longer than 120 s inside the waiting window and fewer than six fixes in it - and no fix reports an accuracy, so under POL-NS-02 it establishes neither arrival nor absence. It is silent, not contrary, and the finding does not rest on it alone: the arrival and waiting facts are carried independently by the trip record and the chat log, each at full weight, so the ruling is not limited to the trace's 0.6 weight and the case does not escalate under POL-NS-09(e). The amount is where the charge fails. The fee schedule fixes the chargeable fee as the greater of the STANDARD zone fee (S$4.00) and the RYDE_X tier fee (S$4.00), i.e. S$4.00. The fare ledger (EV-FARE-00901) charged S$5.00, which does not reconcile; it is impaired under POL-NS-08(d) (weight 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD). The rider is therefore refunded S$1.00 and the correct S$4.00 fee stands. Under POL-NS-07 the driver is compensated at 80% of the S$4.00 fee, i.e. S$3.20, funded by the platform. The anti-farming check is undecidable because driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d and completed_trips_30d are null; undecidable is not adverse, so compensation is paid. The rider's refund and the driver's compensation are independent and are not netted against each other. Confidence is 0.75, limited by the impaired fare breakdown, the weakest artifact carrying a fact the ruling uses; it is above the 0.70 floor, so no escalation. Several claims were discarded on the audit for citing impaired artifacts without naming the issue codes (see the audit record); they do not change the outcome. No referral is produced: no clause in this category directs one on these facts. Open question left in the explanation rather than a referral: the anti-farming check could not be run because the two required driver figures are missing.",
    "referrals_note": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "POL-NS-05 is not engaged. The record does not show the 08:43:00 marker was false: no evidence ties that marker to a position more than 300 m from the pin or to motion at 15 km/h or above, and the trace's closest recorded approach is at the pin itself (min_distance_m 0.0 m, on the impaired trace at weight 0.6). Limb (iii) confirms that even a sloppy marker does not by itself void the fee where the driver then genuinely waits the full period, which the complete chat log shows he did.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason": "Rests on EV-GPS-00901 (weight_multiplier 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD) but, while calling the trace 'impaired', does not name the issue codes that fired, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires. Discarded on the citation check."
    },
    {
      "claim": "None of POL-NS-09's triggers fires. Trigger (c) needs two or more no-show disputes between this same rider and driver in 90 days, and both disputes_with_counterparty_90d fields are null; trigger (d)'s anti-farming test and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d are null; trigger (b) is not met because the trip record and the chat log agree on arrival and wait, and the impaired trace is silent on presence rather than contradicting them. The deciding fact is not carried solely by impaired evidence, so POL-NS-09(e) does not bite either: the complete chat log independently records the arrival and the full waiting window at weight 1.0.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason": "Cites EV-GPS-00901 (weight_multiplier 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD) and refers to it as 'the impaired trace' but does not name the issue codes, contrary to POL-GEN-02(1). Discarded on the citation check."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The rider's assertion that he waited at the lobby is unsupported by any evidence he filed: the trace carries no rider track at all (derived.rider_presence.available false, rider_fix_count 0) and the chat log records no rider message and no answer to the driver's call. Under POL-NS-04(c) the absent rider track is neutral and the driver does not ask the Judge to infer the rider was elsewhere; the point is that the contemporaneous record here is the driver's alone, and it shows him doing everything the platform asks of a driver at this pickup - arriving, messaging twice with a description and plate, calling, waiting, and warning before he cancelled.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason": "Rests on EV-GPS-00901 (weight_multiplier 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD) without disclosing that the artifact is impaired or naming the issue codes, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires. Discarded on the citation check."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The driver cannot repair the shortfall by summing separate in-geofence intervals either. POL-NS-06(i) permits accumulation only where a traffic_advisory that is present and populated, of an admissible type and covering the pickup road and waiting period, shows that holding position was not lawfully possible. EV-ADVIS-00901-01 is MISSING: it carries weight 0.0 and no payload. Limb (i) is therefore unavailable and the whole 300.0 second shortfall stands; the absence of the advisory is itself citable, and nothing in this record could excuse the shortfall.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason": "Discloses the MISSING traffic advisory (weight 0.0) but rests on the GPS-derived shortfall from EV-GPS-00901 (weight_multiplier 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD) without disclosing that impairment or naming its issue codes, contrary to POL-GEN-02(1). Discarded on the citation check."
    },
    {
      "claim": "If the judge concludes that the deciding fact - that the driver held no qualifying in-geofence dwell - rests solely on EV-GPS-00901, then POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at that artifact's 0.60, below the 0.70 floor, and the case escalates under POL-NS-09 rather than leaving the charge in place; an escalated fee is held, not collected or refunded, so the rider is not made to fund a dispute the platform has not resolved. POL-NS-09(e) is the trigger: the sole evidence for the deciding fact would be impaired under POL-NS-08. On either route the rider is not left paying a fee the driver's own telemetry cannot support.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason": "Cites EV-GPS-00901 (weight_multiplier 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD) and EV-FARE-00901 (weight_multiplier 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD) but names the issue codes for neither artifact, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires. Discarded on the citation check."
    }
  ]
}
